{
  "id": "urn:visionflow:page:agent-loop",
  "title": "Agent Loop",
  "slug": "agent-loop",
  "public": true,
  "classIri": "urn:ngm:class:agent-loop",
  "domain": "ai",
  "definition": "The agent loop is the repeating control cycle \u2014 observe, plan, act, evaluate \u2014 through which an autonomous agent perceives its environment, selects a next action or tool call, executes it, and incorporates the result before repeating. It is the core execution pattern underlying agentic systems, terminal coding agents, and retrieval-augmented reasoning, continuing until a termination condition such as task completion or a step budget is reached. The loop's design governs how an agent balances exploration, tool use, and convergence toward a goal.",
